00:41:28,308 --> 00:41:29,549
[SPEAKER_00]: They're always going to those.

618
00:41:30,569 --> 00:41:38,434
[SPEAKER_00]: And the doorbell rang, and I don't know whether it was her daughter-in-law that was there and went and said, there's Tommy Hall here to see you.

619
00:41:38,961 --> 00:41:41,402
[SPEAKER_00]: She said I probably passed out then and there.

620
00:41:41,762 --> 00:41:43,983
[SPEAKER_00]: So I got out and put a rope on and went in here.

621
00:41:44,003 --> 00:41:45,063
[SPEAKER_00]: It was him and his wife.

622
00:41:46,283 --> 00:41:49,064
[SPEAKER_00]: And she said I just didn't know how to tell him he was going to take it.

623
00:41:50,385 --> 00:41:52,986
[SPEAKER_00]: And she said I was hoping he wouldn't come in.

624
00:41:54,386 --> 00:42:01,008
[SPEAKER_00]: But she said he was dying of cancer, this doctor, and he wanted to see her before he died.

625
00:42:01,028 --> 00:42:02,889
[SPEAKER_02]: There was a doctor?

626
00:42:02,929 --> 00:42:06,850
[SPEAKER_00]: There was a colonel in the Air Force and he was dying of cancer.

627
00:42:08,720 --> 00:42:09,981
[SPEAKER_02]: A guy she didn't marry.

628
00:42:10,021 --> 00:42:12,483
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, and he wasn't here before he died.

629
00:42:14,525 --> 00:42:18,167
[SPEAKER_02]: Kind of a morbid purpose.

630
00:42:18,187 --> 00:42:21,230
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, we took him another couple of years to die.

